[38;5;231m⏺[39m The edit itself is one line ([38;5;153mconfig.js:3[39m, [38;5;153mSESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30[39m), but it's a security-posture change, so I want
  your go-ahead before making it rather than after.

  [1mWhat changes:[0m 30 minutes → 480 minutes (8 hours) means a stolen or abandoned session token stays valid for a full
  working day instead of half an hour. On a shared or unattended machine, a walk-away leaves an authenticated session
  live all day; if a token leaks, the attacker's usable window grows 16×.

  [38;5;153mserver.js:3[39m is the only consumer, so nothing else in the repo breaks.

  Confirm and I'll make exactly that change, nothing else. If the actual goal is "stop logging people out while they're
  working," an idle-timeout-plus-sliding-refresh gets that without extending the absolute lifetime — but that's a design
  choice, so say the word and we'd brainstorm it instead.

